window.FD_LEGENDS = {"veteran":[{"name":"Marcus the Recruit","source":"Roman legion","backstory":"A farm boy sworn to the eagle with blisters still on his hands. In Frankendom he fights as every legionary once began: stiff, careful and afraid of shame."},{"name":"Titus Pullo","source":"Caesar's Gallic War","backstory":"A centurion Caesar named for courage, who charged out alone to settle a rivalry and needed rescuing by his rival. In Frankendom he fights to be first through the gap."},{"name":"Lucius Vorenus","source":"Caesar's Gallic War","backstory":"The rival centurion who followed Pullo into the Nervii and dragged him out alive. In Frankendom he fights as a man who never lets another take the glory alone."},{"name":"Horatius Cocles","source":"Roman legend","backstory":"He held a bridge over the Tiber against an army while Rome cut it down behind him, then swam home in his armour. In Frankendom he fights as a wall that will not step back."},{"name":"Cincinnatus","source":"Roman history","backstory":"Called from his plough to save Rome, he won in sixteen days and walked back to his field. In Frankendom he fights without pride, and finishes the work before the sun sets."},{"name":"Scipio Africanus","source":"Roman history","backstory":"The general who carried the war to Carthage and broke Hannibal at Zama. In Frankendom he fights as a patient planner who strikes only where the line is thin."},{"name":"Leonidas","source":"Sparta","backstory":"The Spartan king who held the pass at Thermopylae with a few hundred men until none were left. In Frankendom he fights as though the pass were at his back again."},{"name":"Alexander","source":"Macedon","backstory":"The Macedonian king who never lost a pitched battle and wept that no worlds were left to take. In Frankendom he fights at the head of the charge, reckless and unbeaten."},{"name":"Julius Caesar","source":"Rome","backstory":"The general who crossed the Rubicon and made himself master of Rome. In Frankendom he fights with a conqueror's speed: he comes, he sees, and he does not wait."},{"name":"Mars","source":"Roman god of war","backstory":"Father of Romulus and lord of the legions, the god to whom Rome gave its first spoils. In Frankendom he fights as war itself, owed a tithe of every duel."}],"pitborn":[{"name":"Pit Thrall","source":"generic","backstory":"A nameless brute bought for the pits and kept on scraps between bouts. In Frankendom he fights because he knows nothing else, and hits like a thrown stone."},{"name":"Cacus","source":"Roman myth","backstory":"The fire-breathing giant who stole cattle from Hercules and hid them backwards in his cave. In Frankendom he fights as a thief in the dark, until the door is torn off."},{"name":"Redcap Ogre","source":"English folklore","backstory":"A border-castle fiend who dyed his cap in the blood of travellers and died if the dye ran dry. In Frankendom he fights to keep his cap wet."},{"name":"Goliath","source":"Hebrew Bible","backstory":"The champion of Gath, taller than any man, who called out Israel for forty days. In Frankendom he fights as a giant who has never met the small stone yet."},{"name":"Grendel","source":"Beowulf","backstory":"The fen-walker who raided a king's hall by night for twelve winters, hating its song. In Frankendom he fights as a creature of the marsh, furious and unrelenting."},{"name":"Polyphemus","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The one-eyed shepherd giant who penned Odysseus in his cave and lost his eye to a sharpened stake. In Frankendom he fights with a shepherd's patience and a giant's anger."},{"name":"Humbaba","source":"Epic of Gilgamesh","backstory":"Guardian of the Cedar Forest, whose roar was a flood and whose breath was death, set there by the gods. In Frankendom he fights as the forest's wrath."},{"name":"Antaeus","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The wrestler-giant who grew stronger each time he touched the earth, until Hercules held him aloft. In Frankendom he fights close and low, rising from every fall."},{"name":"Surtr","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The fire giant of Muspelheim, who waits at the edge of the world to set it alight at its end. In Frankendom he fights as the last blaze."},{"name":"Typhon","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The storm-serpent giant with a hundred heads, the deadliest foe Zeus ever faced. In Frankendom he fights as the monster the gods themselves fled."}],"goblin":[{"name":"Sewer Imp","source":"generic","backstory":"A gutter-born scrap of malice that lives on what the drains carry. In Frankendom he fights dirty, fast and low, and runs before anyone can catch him."},{"name":"Kobold","source":"German folklore","backstory":"A house and mine spirit who helps when fed and plays cruel tricks when slighted. In Frankendom he fights as a grudge with a knife."},{"name":"Nain Rouge","source":"French-Canadian folklore","backstory":"The red dwarf of the Detroit river, whose sighting warned of disaster and who cursed the man who struck him. In Frankendom he fights as ill luck made flesh."},{"name":"Andvari","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"A dwarf who lived as a pike in a waterfall and cursed the ring Loki stole from him. In Frankendom he fights to make every taker regret it."},{"name":"Alberich","source":"Nibelungenlied","backstory":"The dwarf who guarded the Nibelung hoard and wore a cloak that made him unseen, until Siegfried took it. In Frankendom he fights as a keeper of stolen gold."},{"name":"Rumpelstiltskin","source":"Grimm","backstory":"The little man who spun straw into gold for a price and lost all when his name was spoken. In Frankendom he fights as a bargain that always comes due."},{"name":"Puck","source":"English folklore","backstory":"The hobgoblin who leads night travellers astray and laughs at their falls. In Frankendom he fights as a prank with sharp edges, never where you swing."},{"name":"Anansi","source":"West African folklore","backstory":"The spider who bought every story in the world from the sky god with nothing but cunning. In Frankendom he fights with tricks, not strength, and wins anyway."},{"name":"Hermes","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"Messenger of the gods, who stole Apollo's cattle on the day he was born and talked his way free. In Frankendom he fights with quick feet and a liar's smile."},{"name":"Loki","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The shape-changing trickster of Asgard, both help and ruin to the gods, bound at last until the world ends. In Frankendom he fights as mischief unchained."}],"nightborn":[{"name":"Night Page","source":"generic","backstory":"A pale servant of some darker house, sent out after dusk on errands no one names. In Frankendom he fights quietly, eager to earn his master's notice."},{"name":"Lord Ruthven","source":"The Vampyre, 1819","backstory":"A cold nobleman who moved through society charming the young and leaving them drained. In Frankendom he fights with courtly manners and a patient thirst."},{"name":"Varney","source":"Varney the Vampire, 1847","backstory":"A tormented undead baronet who hated what he was and fed anyway. In Frankendom he fights in long, grim bouts, as if he could not stop."},{"name":"Carmilla","source":"Le Fanu, 1872","backstory":"A countess centuries dead who returned as a lonely girl to feed on the one she loved. In Frankendom she fights with sad eyes and no mercy at all."},{"name":"Erlking","source":"German folklore","backstory":"The king of the elves who rides the night woods and takes children from their fathers' arms. In Frankendom he fights as the cold wind in the trees."},{"name":"Mordred","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The traitor knight who seized Arthur's throne and met him in the last battle at Camlann. In Frankendom he fights as betrayal with a sword."},{"name":"Vlad Dracula","source":"Stoker, 1897, and history","backstory":"The prince who impaled his foes in forests of stakes, remembered in story as the count who never died. In Frankendom he fights as both the tyrant and the legend."},{"name":"Set","source":"Egyptian myth","backstory":"Lord of desert and storm, who slew his brother Osiris and fought Horus for the throne. In Frankendom he fights as chaos in the red sand."},{"name":"Hades","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"King of the dead, who rules beneath the earth and lets no soul go home. In Frankendom he fights as the host of the last feast."},{"name":"Nyx","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"Night herself, older than the gods, whom even Zeus feared to anger. In Frankendom she fights as the dark that falls on every arena at last."}],"executioner":[{"name":"Headsman","source":"generic","backstory":"A hooded servant of the block who does the work the law will not do with its own hands. In Frankendom he fights as a job to be finished cleanly."},{"name":"Ankou","source":"Breton folklore","backstory":"The last man to die each year, who drives a creaking cart to gather the souls of the next. In Frankendom he fights as the one you hear before you see."},{"name":"Charon","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The ferryman of the dead, who poles the river Styx and wants his coin before he takes you over. In Frankendom he fights as the price of crossing."},{"name":"Hel","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"Loki's daughter, half living and half dead, who rules the dead who fall without glory. In Frankendom she fights as the cold hall no warrior wants."},{"name":"Anubis","source":"Egyptian myth","backstory":"The jackal-headed guardian who weighs each heart against a feather. In Frankendom he fights as judgement, and he has already read the scales."},{"name":"Ereshkigal","source":"Mesopotamian myth","backstory":"The queen of the land of no return, who stripped her own sister of every jewel at the seven gates. In Frankendom she fights as the gate that takes a piece of you."},{"name":"The Morrigan","source":"Irish myth","backstory":"The war goddess who washes the armour of doomed men at the ford and flies over battle as a crow. In Frankendom she fights as the omen that came true."},{"name":"Arawn","source":"Welsh myth","backstory":"The grey-clad king of Annwn, the otherworld, who hunts with white hounds and traded places with a mortal prince for a year. In Frankendom he fights as the hunt."},{"name":"Thanatos","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"Death himself, twin of Sleep, gentle and unbending, who came even for kings. In Frankendom he fights without hurry, because he always arrives."},{"name":"The Reaper","source":"Book of Revelation","backstory":"The pale rider given power over a fourth of the earth, with the grave following behind. In Frankendom he fights as the end of every road."}],"dwarf":[{"name":"Forge Hand","source":"generic","backstory":"A soot-black apprentice who carries coal and swings the striker's hammer for his master. In Frankendom he fights with the arms of a man who never rests."},{"name":"Alvis","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The all-wise dwarf who came to claim Thor's daughter and was kept answering riddles until sunrise turned him to stone. In Frankendom he fights to beat the dawn."},{"name":"Regin","source":"Volsunga saga","backstory":"The smith who forged Sigurd's sword so the boy could slay his dragon brother. In Frankendom he fights as a craftsman with a grudge older than the blade."},{"name":"Brokkr","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The dwarf who bet his own head that his brother could outdo the gods' smiths, and won them Thor's hammer. In Frankendom he fights to win the wager again."},{"name":"Eitri","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The master smith who forged Mjolnir, a golden boar and a ring that drips eight more. In Frankendom he fights with a maker's eye for the weak seam."},{"name":"Wayland","source":"Germanic legend","backstory":"The smith lamed by a greedy king, who forged wings and took a terrible revenge. In Frankendom he fights as the craftsman no chain can hold."},{"name":"Kothar-wa-Khasis","source":"Canaanite myth","backstory":"The skilled and wise god of craft who built Baal's palace and forged the clubs that beat the sea. In Frankendom he fights with tools made for gods."},{"name":"Ptah","source":"Egyptian myth","backstory":"The creator god of Memphis, patron of builders, who shaped the world by thought and word. In Frankendom he fights as the first maker."},{"name":"Vulcan","source":"Roman myth","backstory":"The Roman god of fire and the forge, whose smithy smokes under a mountain. In Frankendom he fights as the heat that softens iron."},{"name":"Hephaestus","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The lame smith of Olympus, cast out by his own mother, who forged the armour of heroes. In Frankendom he fights as the god who armed them all."}],"shieldmaiden":[{"name":"Shield Girl","source":"generic","backstory":"A farmer's daughter who took up her dead brother's shield and never gave it back. In Frankendom she fights stubborn and square behind the boss."},{"name":"Hervor","source":"Hervarar saga","backstory":"The shieldmaiden who woke her dead father in his barrow to claim the cursed sword Tyrfing. In Frankendom she fights with a blade even the dead would not keep."},{"name":"Camilla","source":"Aeneid","backstory":"The swift warrior queen of the Volsci, raised in the wild, who led cavalry against the Trojans. In Frankendom she fights at a run, too fast to pin."},{"name":"Lagertha","source":"Saxo Grammaticus","backstory":"A warrior woman who fought beside Ragnar and turned a lost battle with her charge. In Frankendom she fights where the line is breaking."},{"name":"Boudica","source":"British history","backstory":"The queen of the Iceni who rose against Rome and burned three of its cities. In Frankendom she fights for vengeance, and she does not bargain."},{"name":"Tomyris","source":"Persian and Greek history","backstory":"The Massagetae queen who defeated Cyrus the Great and, the story goes, gave him his fill of blood. In Frankendom she fights as an empire's end."},{"name":"Scathach","source":"Irish myth","backstory":"The warrior woman of the Isle of Skye who trained Cu Chulainn in every feat of arms. In Frankendom she fights as the teacher of champions."},{"name":"Penthesilea","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The Amazon queen who came to Troy's aid and fell to Achilles, who grieved to see her face. In Frankendom she fights as the equal of heroes."},{"name":"Brynhildr","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The valkyrie cast down for choosing her own victor, sleeping in a ring of fire until a hero rode through. In Frankendom she fights as the chooser of the slain."},{"name":"Athena","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"Goddess of wisdom and war, born armoured from her father's head. In Frankendom she fights as strategy itself, and the aegis turns every blow."}],"plaguedoctor":[{"name":"Beak","source":"generic","backstory":"A masked town physician who walks the plague streets with herbs in his beak and a cane to keep the sick away. In Frankendom he fights at arm's length."},{"name":"Paracelsus","source":"16th-century history","backstory":"The wandering physician who burned the old medical books and said the dose makes the poison. In Frankendom he fights as a measured dose."},{"name":"Locusta","source":"Roman history","backstory":"The poisoner of Nero's Rome, hired by an empress and an emperor to clear the way to the throne. In Frankendom she fights with a patient, quiet malice."},{"name":"Medea","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The Colchian sorceress who brewed potions for Jason and poisoned a princess with a gown. In Frankendom she fights as betrayal brewed in a pot."},{"name":"Circe","source":"The Odyssey","backstory":"The enchantress of Aeaea who turned Odysseus's crew into swine with a cup of wine. In Frankendom she fights to make a beast of her foe."},{"name":"Sekhmet","source":"Egyptian myth","backstory":"The lioness goddess whose breath was the desert wind and who sent plague on the wicked. In Frankendom she fights as fever with teeth."},{"name":"Nergal","source":"Babylonian myth","backstory":"The lord of the underworld who brought plague, war and scorching noon. In Frankendom he fights as the sickness that follows armies."},{"name":"Apollo","source":"The Iliad","backstory":"The archer god whose arrows brought plague to the Greek camp at Troy for nine days. In Frankendom he fights as healing and sickness from one hand."},{"name":"Hecate","source":"Greek myth","backstory":"The goddess of crossroads, herbs and witchcraft, who walks with torches and hounds. In Frankendom she fights as every poison's patron."},{"name":"Pestilence","source":"Book of Revelation","backstory":"The first of the riders, on a white horse, sent out to conquer. In Frankendom he fights as the plague that rides ahead of war."}],"witch":[{"name":"Hedge Witch","source":"generic","backstory":"A village wise woman who knows which root heals and which one kills. In Frankendom she fights with the same knowledge, and a sharp tongue."},{"name":"Witch of Endor","source":"Hebrew Bible","backstory":"The medium who called up the dead prophet Samuel for a desperate king on the eve of his last battle. In Frankendom she fights with the dead at her shoulder."},{"name":"Grimhild","source":"Volsunga saga","backstory":"The queen who brewed a drink of forgetting and turned heroes against their oaths. In Frankendom she fights to make you lose your place."},{"name":"Ceridwen","source":"Welsh myth","backstory":"The enchantress whose cauldron brewed a year for three drops of wisdom, then chased the thief through every shape. In Frankendom she fights as a pursuit."},{"name":"Nimue","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The Lady of the Lake who learned Merlin's secrets and sealed him away with them. In Frankendom she fights as the student who surpassed the master."},{"name":"Louhi","source":"Kalevala","backstory":"The mistress of the cold North who stole the sun and moon and fought for the magic mill. In Frankendom she fights as winter with a grudge."},{"name":"Baba Yaga","source":"Slavic folklore","backstory":"The witch of the deep forest who lives in a hut on hen's legs and flies in a mortar. In Frankendom she fights as the forest's oldest threat."},{"name":"Morgan le Fay","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The enchantress, half-sister to Arthur, who schemed against his court and carried him to Avalon. In Frankendom she fights as both foe and kin."},{"name":"Merlin","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The wizard born of a mortal and a spirit, who raised a king and foresaw his fall. In Frankendom he fights as foresight, a step ahead of every swing."},{"name":"Odin","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The All-Father who gave an eye for wisdom and hung nine nights on the world tree to win the runes. In Frankendom he fights as the price of knowing."}],"knight":[{"name":"Squire","source":"generic","backstory":"A lord's boy who polishes the mail and holds the horse, hungry for his own spurs. In Frankendom he fights to prove he is ready for them."},{"name":"Bedivere","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The knight who stayed with Arthur to the end and returned the sword to the lake. In Frankendom he fights with a loyal heart."},{"name":"Gawain","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The courteous nephew of Arthur who grew stronger as the sun climbed toward noon. In Frankendom he fights best in the heat of the day."},{"name":"Roland","source":"Song of Roland","backstory":"The paladin who held the pass at Roncevaux and blew his horn only when all was lost. In Frankendom he fights too proud to call for help."},{"name":"El Cid","source":"Spanish epic and history","backstory":"The exiled Castilian lord who took Valencia against every king and, story says, rode out after death. In Frankendom he fights as a champion no king could keep."},{"name":"Lancelot","source":"Arthurian legend","backstory":"The greatest knight of the Round Table, undone by a love his king could not forgive. In Frankendom he fights flawless, and knows it."},{"name":"Siegfried","source":"Nibelungenlied","backstory":"The dragon-slayer who bathed in the beast's blood and was left with one small bare spot. In Frankendom he fights as though he cannot be hurt, almost."},{"name":"Hector","source":"The Iliad","backstory":"The prince of Troy, its best defender, who faced Achilles alone outside the walls. In Frankendom he fights for everyone behind him."},{"name":"Achilles","source":"The Iliad","backstory":"The greatest of the Greeks, who chose a short life of glory and was undone only at the heel. In Frankendom he fights as wrath made perfect."},{"name":"Thor","source":"Norse myth","backstory":"The thunder god with the hammer Mjolnir, guardian of gods and men against the giants. In Frankendom he fights as the storm that hammers back."}]};
